# Copy to .env.  ->  cp lab/.env.sample lab/.env
#
# FOUR VALUES BELOW ARE PLACEHOLDERS. REPLACE THEM with your own tenant's.
# They are wrapped in <angle brackets> so nothing can use them by accident: for the three the lab
# reads, it refuses to start and names whichever are still unset, rather than quietly signing in
# somewhere you are not. The fourth, FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT, only records where your deployment lives.
#
# Where each comes from is in Chapter 1 of the book: "Creating the Microsoft Foundry resources"
# for the Foundry values, "Creating the Dataverse environment" for the Dataverse pair.
#
# Model calls are KEYLESS: they reuse your Fraud Desk sign-in (python m3_login.py, or for C#
# dotnet run -- login), the same session that reads the claims book. There is no key to paste.

# --------------------------------------------------------------- Microsoft Foundry
# Your AI Services account's endpoint. No lab code reads this one - it is here so the file
# records where the deployment lives.
FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT=https://<your-foundry-account>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/

# KEYLESS BY DEFAULT: leave this line exactly as it is. Paste a real value ONLY to override
# the sign-in - your own resource's key, or a token you minted yourself:
#   az account get-access-token --resource https://cognitiveservices.azure.com --query accessToken -o tsv
# Whatever is here is sent as "Authorization: Bearer <value>", which is why a key and a token
# are interchangeable. A pasted token expires after about 60 to 90 minutes; a key does not.
FOUNDRY_KEY=<leave-as-is-for-keyless-or-paste-your-own>

# The deployment NAME you chose in the Azure portal. Chapter 1 has you name it exactly
# this, so leave it alone unless you called yours something else.
MODEL_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-5-mini

# The Agent Framework base_url. The same account as FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT, plus the /openai/v1/
# suffix - required for gpt-5, and the trailing slash is not optional.
FOUNDRY_OPENAI_V1=https://<your-foundry-account>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/openai/v1/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- Dataverse (the Fraud Desk)
# WHICH TENANT YOU SIGN IN TO, AND WHICH ENVIRONMENT YOU READ.
#
# Neither is a secret. A tenant id and an org URL identify a directory and a database; they grant
# nothing on their own, and you still have to sign in as yourself and hold a role. They are here
# rather than in the source so that pointing the lab at a different environment is a config change
# instead of a code edit.
#
# Your tenant id is on the Entra ID overview page. The org URL is your Dataverse environment's,
# ending .crm<n>.dynamics.com - the Power Platform admin centre shows it against the environment.
# You also need the Fraud Desk tables and the security role in that environment; both arrive with
# the setup pack in Tenant-Setup/ (Chapter 1).
DATAVERSE_TENANT=<your-tenant-id>
DATAVERSE_ORG=https://<your-environment>.crm4.dynamics.com
